# Project Rules

## Rust Formatting Checks

After modifying Rust code, you must pass the formatting check:

```bash
cargo fmt --all --check
```

If the check fails due to formatting issues, run the following commands to fix them, then confirm that the check passes:

```bash
cargo fmt --all
cargo fmt --all --check
```

The formatting check is complete only when `cargo fmt --all --check` exits without errors.

## Rust Clippy Checks

After modifying Rust code, you must also run Clippy in addition to the formatting check, treating all warnings as errors:

```bash
cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
```

If the check fails, fix all errors and warnings, then run the command again to confirm that it passes.

Code changes are complete only after both `cargo fmt --all --check` and `cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` exit without errors.
